      "content": "thanks for this. it's a good start, but looking at the sentiment score on my end for that draft, it came back a bit low—the tool thinks it's a bit too \"heavy\" or negative because of the words \"outage\", \"frustration\", and \"failure\". \n\ncan we try a version that feels a bit more positive/constructive? i still need it to be professional and not ignore the problem, but maybe we can pivot the tone so it's less about the \"failure\" and more about the \"improvement\" and \"solutions\" so the sentiment score stays in a healthier range? we don't want it to be fake, just... more upbeat about the resolution?",
